<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What a Joomla site reads when its administrator presses "Check For Updates" for the Tracy
    template.

    Reached because `templateDetails.xml` declares this address as the template's update server.
    Joomla records that address when the template is INSTALLED, so a site that got the template
    before this file existed has no update site and must be updated once by hand (or by Tracy)
    before it can update itself.

    One entry per released version, newest first. Joomla picks the highest version whose
    targetplatform matches the site it runs on, so leaving old entries in place costs nothing.

    Written by scripts/release-joomla-template.mjs, which puts the same number here and in the
    manifest inside the zip.
-->
<updates>
</updates>
